  "reason": [
    "k=60 and equal layer weights are kept: no point of the grid improves the criteria with a different k or weight and the measure does not justify changing them (a larger k makes the same bonus overturn more ranks; k=100 already breaks CA-18 at bonus 0.0002).",
    "The bonus is measured in score units: one rank step at the top is 1/60-1/61 = 0.00027. Up to 0.0002 the bonus only settles ties and near-ties (deep ranks): recall@5 1.0, MRR 0.9715 (CA-18: fused MRR >= the best single layer, overall and per subset), CA-35 met in every subset. Above 0.0002 (0.0003..0.0005) CA-18 fails (MRR 0.9519).",
    "Between 0.0015 and 0.01 the bonus turns validated into a strong preference (recall@5 0.85, MRR 0.82): it still meets the thresholds and CA-35 (bonus 0.003..0.01, identical plateau) but fails CA-18; from 0.02 up it reproduces the old absolute order and fails the gate (recall@5 0.54).",
    "0.0001 is the middle of the interval that meets everything (0 < bonus <= 0.0002; 0.0001 and 0.0002 measure the same on this dataset) instead of its edge, and it is above 0 so a validated hit still wins an exact tie. The dataset has 24 + 24 + 12 + 12 questions of a single synthetic corpus: do not read finer values than the grid as meaningful.",
    "The value is configurable (MEMORY_FUSION_VALIDATED_BONUS, validated at startup in Settings) so an operator who wants validated to weigh more can raise it; the plateau 0.003..0.01 is the documented alternative that still passes the gate thresholds and CA-35 (not CA-18)."
